    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate today as we navigate a matchup against Dylan Cease, whose 2.96 xERA forces a tactical retreat in our expected output. Our primary exposure relies on **Andy Pages** (43.41) and **Drake Baldwin** (40.51). **Andy Pages** remains a marginal play; despite being relegated to the #8 spot, his recent form provides a slight floor, though his production is cannibalized by the elite efficiency of the opposing arm. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** faces the same uphill climb from the bottom of the order. Given the scarcity of our stolen base targets today\u2014most of our primary speed threats like **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** are absent or benched due to unfavorable splits\u2014we are effectively prioritizing game-cap preservation over aggressive pursuit of volume.\n\nThe benching decisions were straightforward given the team-wide off-day for cornerstones like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, the decision to hold others like **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos** is purely circumstantial. Among the active bench, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Jacob Wilson** were the closest to cracking the starting nine, but their proximity to Cease\u2019s high-strikeout profile pushed their projected scores below the 40-point threshold. We are consciously avoiding high-variance outcomes against a pitcher of Cease\u2019s caliber, preferring to keep the powder dry for upcoming series against weaker rotations. Monitor **Drake Baldwin** closely; if his spot in the lineup shifts upward before first pitch, his floor may see a minor recovery, but for now, we are treating this as a low-intensity day for the roster.",
